  "notes": {
    "type-check": "Decides what is wrong with the promises of the outside world and the rows of decision tables.",
    "type-check.calcs.promise": "The promise of a query of the outside world: whether it promises fresh answers, increasing ones, whether it answers integers, and whether it has parameters. The problems, in this order: promising both fresh and increasing; promising increasing answers that are not integers; promising either one for a query with parameters.",
    "type-check.calcs.row": "A row of a decision table: whether it is the last row, whether its condition is otherwise, whether every cell is a constant, and whether it has the same columns as the first row. The problems, in this order: the last row is not otherwise; otherwise is not the last row; a cell is not a constant; the columns differ."
  },
